Split-path swtpm NVRAM backend for multi-host TPM.

Routes "permall" (persistent keys/certs) to a shared directory (CephFS)
and all other state (volatilestate, savestate) to a local tmpfs directory.
No session-level lock — only a brief flock during permall writes.

This enables concurrent swtpm instances on multiple hosts sharing the
same TPM identity without lock contention from the dir:// backend.

URI format: seed:///path/to/shared/dir
Volatile dir: SWTPM_SEED_VOLATILE_DIR env var

